1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:12,067
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,933 --> 00:00:32,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:35,467
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,933 --> 00:00:41,467
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,433 --> 00:00:44,500
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:45,500
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:46,767
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:48,900
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,433 --> 00:00:51,433
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:53,767
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,467 --> 00:00:55,967
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,800
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:59,667 --> 00:01:00,833
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,833 --> 00:01:03,433
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:06,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:09,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:11,533
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:12,033 --> 00:01:13,533
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,533 --> 00:01:14,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,133 --> 00:01:23,633
<i>I want to honor you all
for a job well done.</i>

21
00:01:23,633 --> 00:01:25,500
<i> - For Sam!
</i>- [IN UNISON]  For Sam!

22
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:26,700
<i>- For Sam!
- [GUN SHOTS]</i>

23
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:28,000
- Enough! Mission accomplished!
<i> - Let's go!</i>

24
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,533
<i> We were targeted!</i>

25
00:01:29,533 --> 00:01:31,533
<i> The Zafras are behind this!</i>

26
00:01:31,533 --> 00:01:34,167
<i>We can't lose anyone else
because of the Zafras!</i>

27
00:01:34,167 --> 00:01:37,167
<i>The Zafras will pay for what
they did to the NCIA.</i>

28
00:01:37,167 --> 00:01:40,500
<i>You have to wear white
to look decent.</i>

29
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:41,833
<i> This jacket looks good.</i>

30
00:01:41,867 --> 00:01:43,867
<i>Tomorrow, I promise you,
I won't come home</i>

31
00:01:43,867 --> 00:01:45,567
<i> without getting a job.</i>

32
00:01:45,567 --> 00:01:50,033
<i>Any woman you'll truly love
will surely be blessed.</i>

33
00:01:51,833 --> 00:01:53,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

34
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:54,967
[TIRES SCREECHING]

35
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:58,033
They're here.

36
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:04,733
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

37
00:02:04,733 --> 00:02:05,867
How did it go?

38
00:02:05,933 --> 00:02:08,167
[CHUCKLES WRYLY]
They were no match for us, Ma.

39
00:02:10,033 --> 00:02:15,667
And now they know we're not
to be messed with.

40
00:02:16,967 --> 00:02:19,533
[DEBORAH]
If they mess with our family,

41
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:21,733
we'll get them back.

42
00:02:25,533 --> 00:02:26,600
Pa!

43
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:30,767
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

44
00:02:30,767 --> 00:02:31,700
Pa!

45
00:02:38,967 --> 00:02:41,633
[FOOTSTEPS RECEDING]

46
00:02:41,633 --> 00:02:43,200
[PHONE RINGING]

47
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:44,167
Yes?

48
00:02:46,767 --> 00:02:47,867
I'll tell her.

49
00:02:49,167 --> 00:02:50,133
Oh, okay.

50
00:02:51,267 --> 00:02:53,933
Ma'am, Ms. Catacutan called.

51
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:55,967
- What did she say?
- She wants to be picked up.

52
00:02:56,633 --> 00:02:57,933
Okay, have someone pick her up.

53
00:02:57,933 --> 00:02:58,933
Yes, ma'am.

54
00:02:58,933 --> 00:03:04,767
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

55
00:03:04,767 --> 00:03:05,967
Good job, son.

56
00:03:08,233 --> 00:03:09,467
Thank you, Ma.

57
00:03:17,633 --> 00:03:21,033
Tonight, the Zafras
have succeeded.

58
00:03:21,667 --> 00:03:23,767
Go on, get some rest.

59
00:03:23,767 --> 00:03:25,167
[IN UNISON] Yes, boss!

60
00:03:25,167 --> 00:03:31,700
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

61
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:32,733
[DOOR OPENS]

62
00:03:34,033 --> 00:03:38,000
[HEART MONITOR BEEPING]

63
00:03:40,767 --> 00:03:41,900
- Doc.
- Hey.

64
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:43,833
How is he?

65
00:03:44,633 --> 00:03:46,733
He lost a lot of blood.

66
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:49,667
Good thing we got him here
right away.

67
00:03:49,667 --> 00:03:51,600
But don't worry, we're keeping
a close eye on him,

68
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:53,700
and he should be fine.

69
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:56,033
Okay, I'll leave you guys
for now.

70
00:03:56,067 --> 00:03:57,133
- Thank you, Doc.
- Alright.

71
00:03:57,700 --> 00:03:59,133
- Thank you, Doc.
- [SIGHS DEEPLY]

72
00:04:00,233 --> 00:04:02,167
Those Zafras are unbelievable!

73
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:04,633
They even dragged Sir into this.

74
00:04:06,033 --> 00:04:07,667
What do we do?

75
00:04:07,667 --> 00:04:09,300
We can't just do nothing
about what happened.

76
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,867
We need to strike back.

77
00:04:10,867 --> 00:04:12,100
Not yet, Borromeo.

78
00:04:12,367 --> 00:04:14,300
There's a right time
and way for that.

79
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:16,233
And all we wanted to do
was pay our respects

80
00:04:16,233 --> 00:04:17,700
to our fallen teammate.

81
00:04:18,033 --> 00:04:20,167
And all of a sudden, this.

82
00:04:20,867 --> 00:04:22,133
What I'm thinking is,

83
00:04:22,133 --> 00:04:25,033
how did they find out
about our tribute dinner?

84
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:26,267
Don't worry.

85
00:04:26,733 --> 00:04:28,767
We won't let this slide.

86
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:32,233
For Sam, for Sir,

87
00:04:32,233 --> 00:04:35,033
and for everyone from the NCIA
who got caught up in this,

88
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:37,633
those criminals will pay.

89
00:04:39,667 --> 00:04:42,700
[VAN HUMMING]

90
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:49,667
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

91
00:04:55,933 --> 00:04:57,200
Why did you ask
to be picked up?

92
00:04:57,867 --> 00:04:59,067
What do you need?

93
00:04:59,067 --> 00:05:00,600
Where's Ma'am Deborah?

94
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:02,167
I need to talk to her.

95
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:03,700
Wait.

96
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:05,367
We'll search you.

97
00:05:05,367 --> 00:05:12,367
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

98
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:22,900
This isn't allowed.

99
00:05:28,133 --> 00:05:29,733
You can't take this
with you either.

100
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:34,267
So you're still alive.

101
00:05:35,467 --> 00:05:37,300
The deal was,

102
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:41,033
you'd attack the NCIA and
I wouldn't get caught in it!

103
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:44,200
Well, you had to go
and be stupid.

104
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:46,267
Come on.

105
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:48,267
[GRUNTS]

106
00:05:49,267 --> 00:05:51,900
Ma'am, Ms. Catacutan is here.

107
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:54,133
What do you want?

108
00:05:55,667 --> 00:05:57,167
I thought we were allies!

109
00:05:57,167 --> 00:06:00,300
We agreed you'd attack
once I had already left!

110
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:02,300
Why did you attack so early?!

111
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:08,167
I was still there when your men
started shooting

112
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:10,067
at my colleagues!

113
00:06:10,967 --> 00:06:13,833
[DEBORAH CHUCKLES]
And yet, here you are.

114
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:19,100
I almost died!

115
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:21,333
Almost.

116
00:06:21,333 --> 00:06:22,333
But you didn't.

117
00:06:23,367 --> 00:06:25,967
When you need information,

118
00:06:25,967 --> 00:06:27,833
you need me there right away.

119
00:06:27,833 --> 00:06:30,833
But when my life
is on the line--

120
00:06:30,833 --> 00:06:32,033
- [EXHALES]
- [GLASS CLINKS]

121
00:06:32,033 --> 00:06:34,100
Don't forget what you are, Pia.

122
00:06:35,167 --> 00:06:36,900
You're not one of us.

123
00:06:38,267 --> 00:06:40,000
You're our pawn.

124
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,767
We're paying you to betray
your colleagues.

125
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:47,833
So don't stand there and
demand loyalty from us.

126
00:06:47,833 --> 00:06:49,233
You have no right--

127
00:06:49,233 --> 00:06:50,467
Right?

128
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,033
[CHUCKLES WRYLY]

129
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:59,500
You sold your soul to us, Pia.

130
00:07:01,067 --> 00:07:04,933
Don't act like you have
any self-respect.

131
00:07:05,733 --> 00:07:07,767
That you deserve any
self-respect.

132
00:07:08,133 --> 00:07:09,433
- [LOUD SLAP]
- [GASPS] Ma!

133
00:07:10,333 --> 00:07:11,500
Ma!

134
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:12,967
Ma, are you alright?

135
00:07:12,967 --> 00:07:19,867
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING, FADES]

136
00:07:22,333 --> 00:07:24,033
Don't touch my lover.

137
00:07:27,933 --> 00:07:30,233
If you hurt Gloria, you'd
better prepare yourselves.

138
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:34,167
No matter where you hide...

139
00:07:35,933 --> 00:07:37,500
I will find you.

140
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:42,033
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

141
00:07:42,033 --> 00:07:43,067
Gloria.

142
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:49,000
Please forgive me.

143
00:07:52,867 --> 00:07:57,433
I didn't want to lie to you.

144
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:04,267
I have to do this
to protect you.

145
00:08:07,733 --> 00:08:09,567
Your life is in danger.

146
00:08:14,267 --> 00:08:16,167
A lot of people want
to kill you.

147
00:08:18,733 --> 00:08:20,067
But don't worry.

148
00:08:21,067 --> 00:08:23,767
I won't let that happen.

149
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:29,700
I'll be the first one
to die for you.

150
00:08:31,833 --> 00:08:33,733
I know...

151
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:38,133
that one of the people
hunting you down is Victor.

152
00:08:39,133 --> 00:08:41,933
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

153
00:08:41,933 --> 00:08:42,767
That's it.

154
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:45,800
Victor Zafra?

155
00:08:46,733 --> 00:08:48,267
How are you
connected to this?

156
00:08:50,767 --> 00:08:52,100
I idolize him.

157
00:08:54,133 --> 00:08:55,133
Victor.

158
00:08:57,767 --> 00:08:58,900
He's good.

159
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:04,067
He's good at throwing punches
and using his gun.

160
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:06,800
What do you have
to do with him?

161
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:09,933
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

162
00:09:09,933 --> 00:09:12,233
I'm watching his movies.

163
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:15,733
He was good in Notoryus.

164
00:09:18,267 --> 00:09:23,300
And his movie
with Cesar Montano, UTOL.

165
00:09:23,867 --> 00:09:25,300
He's amazing.

166
00:09:25,767 --> 00:09:27,333
I idolize them both.

167
00:09:27,333 --> 00:09:34,267
[CURIOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

168
00:09:40,133 --> 00:09:41,967
[GABO] Ah, Gloria...

169
00:09:44,133 --> 00:09:45,400
Don't worry.

170
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:47,433
I won't let anything
happen to you.

171
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:49,700
You know...

172
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:52,200
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

173
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:55,033
I really want
to tell you something.

174
00:09:58,133 --> 00:10:00,700
When I first saw you...

175
00:10:01,733 --> 00:10:03,833
I thought you were a snob...

176
00:10:07,767 --> 00:10:09,133
but now...

177
00:10:12,067 --> 00:10:14,900
I see the beauty of your heart.

178
00:10:18,833 --> 00:10:21,300
You are so kind.

179
00:10:25,033 --> 00:10:27,300
And you're beautiful...

180
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:32,833
I think I'm already falling
in love with you.

181
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:40,067
I'm just too shy to tell you
because you'll reject me.

182
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:44,500
I'm sure...

183
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:48,867
that if you find out
the truth, you'd leave.

184
00:10:53,033 --> 00:10:55,033
Gloria...

185
00:10:56,033 --> 00:10:57,867
I love you.

186
00:11:00,767 --> 00:11:03,100
I love you so much.

187
00:11:06,033 --> 00:11:07,367
Gloria.

188
00:11:09,433 --> 00:11:12,567
Please love me back.

189
00:11:12,567 --> 00:11:19,533
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

190
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:32,133
That was a big mistake.

191
00:11:34,167 --> 00:11:37,633
You know you're not getting
out of here alive, right?

192
00:11:37,633 --> 00:11:42,300
[EERIE MUSIC PLAYING]

193
00:11:42,333 --> 00:11:46,733
[DEBORAH BREATHES HEAVILY]

194
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:53,167
No.

195
00:11:56,133 --> 00:11:57,733
I'll let this pass,

196
00:11:58,867 --> 00:12:02,000
just this once.

197
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,933
But just do
what we told you to do.

198
00:12:04,933 --> 00:12:06,867
You have an obligation to us.

199
00:12:06,867 --> 00:12:09,100
Fix Victor's case

200
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:12,800
so we won't have to
put up with each other anymore!

201
00:12:13,767 --> 00:12:15,667
And don't forget.

202
00:12:17,367 --> 00:12:19,333
I'm your last resort

203
00:12:20,667 --> 00:12:23,967
to get your son out!

204
00:12:23,967 --> 00:12:24,967
[TENSE STING]

205
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:30,300
[DEBORAH] Arturo,
get her out of here

206
00:12:30,300 --> 00:12:32,033
before I change my mind

207
00:12:32,033 --> 00:12:34,367
and she doesn't
make it out alive.

208
00:12:34,367 --> 00:12:36,367
[DEBORAH BREATHING HEAVILY]

209
00:12:36,367 --> 00:12:40,000
[PIA GRUNTING]

210
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:43,033
[FOOTSTEPS RECEDING]

211
00:12:43,033 --> 00:12:45,167
[PIA] You're hurting me!
Let me go!

212
00:12:45,167 --> 00:12:46,967
[PIA BREATHING HEAVILY]

213
00:12:46,967 --> 00:12:47,900
[PIA YELPS]

214
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:50,900
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

215
00:12:50,933 --> 00:12:53,700
Don't ever do that again.

216
00:12:53,700 --> 00:12:54,867
What do you mean?

217
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:58,300
Going against the Zafras.

218
00:12:58,733 --> 00:12:59,700
[BREATHES HEAVILY]

219
00:12:59,900 --> 00:13:01,067
[PIA GRUNTS]

220
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:05,833
I'll do whatever I want.

221
00:13:08,067 --> 00:13:10,733
Learn your place.

222
00:13:10,733 --> 00:13:13,000
If you still want to live,

223
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,200
you don't know
who you're up against.

224
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:19,333
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

225
00:13:19,333 --> 00:13:20,667
[TENSE STING]

226
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:24,933
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [LUCAS GRUNTS]

227
00:13:24,933 --> 00:13:26,367
- [BODY THUDS]
- [LUCAS GROANS]

228
00:13:26,367 --> 00:13:28,233
- Mariano!
- You saw the result

229
00:13:28,233 --> 00:13:29,767
of your stubbornness!

230
00:13:29,767 --> 00:13:31,933
Pa! I just wanted
to prove to them--

231
00:13:31,933 --> 00:13:34,400
You even almost killed
our asset!

232
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:35,967
- [LUCAS GRUNTS]
- [DEBORAH] Mariano!

233
00:13:35,967 --> 00:13:38,267
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

234
00:13:38,267 --> 00:13:40,433
[DEBORAH] We can still
replace Pia.

235
00:13:40,433 --> 00:13:42,033
We really need to.

236
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:44,267
But not now!

237
00:13:44,267 --> 00:13:47,033
Pia is already working
on Victor's case.

238
00:13:47,033 --> 00:13:49,700
Your brother's freedom
is in her hands!

239
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:51,267
If this goes wrong

240
00:13:51,267 --> 00:13:53,233
and Victor doesn't get out,

241
00:13:53,233 --> 00:13:57,000
I'll forget you're my son
and I'll finish you myself!

242
00:13:58,967 --> 00:14:00,167
Get out of here!

243
00:14:00,167 --> 00:14:07,200
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

244
00:14:11,967 --> 00:14:14,733
[DEBORAH BREATHING HEAVILY]

245
00:14:14,733 --> 00:14:16,433
[DEBORAH CRYING]

246
00:14:16,433 --> 00:14:22,300
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC
CONTINUES, FADES]

247
00:14:23,933 --> 00:14:26,733
[EERIE MUSIC PLAYING]

248
00:14:26,733 --> 00:14:28,100
Where's my stuff?

249
00:14:29,033 --> 00:14:29,967
[GUN CLINKS]

250
00:14:33,133 --> 00:14:34,100
[GUN CLINKS]

251
00:14:41,333 --> 00:14:42,333
[GUN CLACKS]

252
00:14:42,333 --> 00:14:49,300
[EERIE MUSIC CONTINUES]

253
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,067
[SOFT RUSTLING]

254
00:14:57,933 --> 00:15:00,967
[SOFT FOOTSTEPS]

255
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:11,033
[VAN ENGINE REVS]

256
00:15:11,033 --> 00:15:12,000
- [VAN DOOR SLAMS]
- [VAN DOOR OPENS]

257
00:15:13,367 --> 00:15:17,967
- [VAN DOOR SLAMS]
- [VAN ENGINE REVS]

258
00:15:17,967 --> 00:15:19,500
[DEBORAH] Pia is starting
to go against us.

259
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:21,800
I've already talked to her.

260
00:15:22,133 --> 00:15:25,500
I want to make sure
she isn't betraying us.

261
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:27,267
What do you want me to do?

262
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:29,067
From now on,

263
00:15:29,067 --> 00:15:32,200
follow her every move.

264
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:34,833
I want to know
where she goes,

265
00:15:34,867 --> 00:15:37,067
who she talks to, everything!

266
00:15:37,333 --> 00:15:38,300
Yes, ma'am.

267
00:15:38,567 --> 00:15:40,033
I'll take care of it.

268
00:15:40,033 --> 00:15:46,967
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

269
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:56,900
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

270
00:15:58,267 --> 00:15:59,233
Mom.

271
00:15:59,833 --> 00:16:00,567
[SOFT GASP]

272
00:16:00,567 --> 00:16:02,733
[ISOBEL SOFTLY EXHALES]

273
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,900
Did you fall asleep, mom?

274
00:16:11,267 --> 00:16:12,233
[SMACKS LIPS]

275
00:16:12,433 --> 00:16:13,400
Barely.

276
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:16,567
So,

277
00:16:17,467 --> 00:16:19,900
are you ready
to go back to work?

278
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:26,067
I have to, don't I?

279
00:16:26,233 --> 00:16:28,600
[MAXINE SOFTLY EXHALES]
Mom, I just want you to know

280
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:30,433
Dad and I are here for you.

281
00:16:30,433 --> 00:16:33,800
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

282
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:35,567
[MAXINE] I know
we're all still grieving.

283
00:16:38,033 --> 00:16:41,000
I know my family is still there.

284
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:45,300
It's just that we're not
complete anymore.

285
00:16:49,900 --> 00:16:50,867
But, mom,

286
00:16:52,333 --> 00:16:53,300
[ISOBEL CRYING]

287
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:56,067
whenever you need someone
to talk to,

288
00:16:56,067 --> 00:16:58,200
Dad and I
are right here for you.

289
00:17:01,900 --> 00:17:04,367
You don't have to be fooled
by that Madam Rosa.

290
00:17:06,933 --> 00:17:08,067
Fooled?

291
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:09,900
[ISOBEL SCOFFS]

292
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:11,233
Max!

293
00:17:12,067 --> 00:17:14,200
Madam Rosa isn't fooling me.

294
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:18,300
They haven't even found
Sam's jacket yet.

295
00:17:18,933 --> 00:17:21,467
She already knows
your sister is gone.

296
00:17:21,467 --> 00:17:23,333
That jacket doesn't
prove anything.

297
00:17:24,867 --> 00:17:26,333
Sam is not dead yet.

298
00:17:27,333 --> 00:17:29,533
I know it's very hard
for you to accept

299
00:17:29,533 --> 00:17:31,767
what happened
to your sister.

300
00:17:33,167 --> 00:17:37,933
You can't imagine what pain
I'm going through right now.

301
00:17:37,933 --> 00:17:43,433
As a mother, I shouldn't be
grieving for my children.

302
00:17:45,933 --> 00:17:46,900
[MAXINE SNIFFLES]

303
00:17:47,133 --> 00:17:50,900
I know that Madam Rosa is real.

304
00:17:53,467 --> 00:17:56,200
And, dear, I know
that you know that too.

305
00:17:56,200 --> 00:18:03,267
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

306
00:18:04,367 --> 00:18:06,333
[PEOPLE CHATTERING
IN BACKGROUND]

307
00:18:06,333 --> 00:18:07,300
[TWINKLE LAUGHS]

308
00:18:09,533 --> 00:18:10,900
Hey!

309
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:13,300
Why are you moping there
so early in the morning?

310
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:15,000
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

311
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,233
Toto!

312
00:18:16,233 --> 00:18:17,233
Hey!

313
00:18:17,233 --> 00:18:18,300
You might end up
like that for good.

314
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:19,300
Come on!

315
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:22,433
Sweetie,

316
00:18:22,900 --> 00:18:25,067
I couldn't sleep last night.

317
00:18:25,067 --> 00:18:27,233
I was thinking about my dreams,

318
00:18:27,233 --> 00:18:29,333
wondering if
I've forgotten them.

319
00:18:29,333 --> 00:18:31,900
You heard Madam Rosa clearly.

320
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:34,833
She said I'm never going
to be rich.

321
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:36,867
What are you talking about?

322
00:18:36,867 --> 00:18:38,000
Come on, Toto.

323
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,200
[TWINKLE BREATHING HEAVILY]

324
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:42,000
Maybe what Madam Rosa
said was fake.

325
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,367
Don't let it affect you.

326
00:18:43,500 --> 00:18:45,233
She was guessing your future.

327
00:18:45,233 --> 00:18:46,667
Guessing.

328
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:49,000
That means it's not sure.

329
00:18:49,567 --> 00:18:50,533
Hmm?

330
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:52,633
[SIGHS] I hope so...

331
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:06,233
[TEKLA] Your appearance won't
change. It'll stay the same.

332
00:19:06,233 --> 00:19:10,033
- Ah!
- Ah! Yes!

333
00:19:10,033 --> 00:19:10,600
[LAUGHTER]

334
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:12,000
That's good.

335
00:19:12,567 --> 00:19:16,233
- [BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]
- [LAUGHTER]

336
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,033
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

337
00:19:20,033 --> 00:19:21,167
Put it in there first!

338
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:22,667
Auntie!

339
00:19:23,133 --> 00:19:26,100
Gloria, look!
They all came!

340
00:19:26,100 --> 00:19:27,633
Hey, good morning!

341
00:19:27,633 --> 00:19:29,167
- Gloria, we are ready!
- We're ready!

342
00:19:30,067 --> 00:19:31,233
Miss Gloria, let's go!

343
00:19:31,967 --> 00:19:34,933
It's amusing that you
guys took me seriously.

344
00:19:34,933 --> 00:19:36,300
Of course, Gloria!

345
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:38,400
Do you think
we just lied to you?

346
00:19:38,400 --> 00:19:39,633
We're not like that.

347
00:19:39,633 --> 00:19:41,033
We are sometimes.

348
00:19:42,233 --> 00:19:43,900
You have a point, Gloria.

349
00:19:43,967 --> 00:19:47,133
If we can fight for our place,
we can clean it up too.

350
00:19:47,133 --> 00:19:50,400
I'd also like to know how much
all that junk will cost me.

351
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:52,933
You're such a gold digger!

352
00:19:53,467 --> 00:19:54,567
Thank you.

353
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:57,267
Alright. Let's begin.

354
00:19:57,267 --> 00:19:58,467
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

355
00:19:58,467 --> 00:20:00,233
[TEKLA] Don't
involve me in this.

356
00:20:00,233 --> 00:20:01,233
I'm fine.

357
00:20:01,233 --> 00:20:02,600
[BINOY] Let's help
each other out!

358
00:20:02,633 --> 00:20:03,967
I don't live here.

359
00:20:03,967 --> 00:20:05,500
- I was on the other side!
- It's Gabo!

360
00:20:08,967 --> 00:20:15,967
[BRIGHT UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

361
00:20:38,633 --> 00:20:39,967
Mm!

362
00:20:41,667 --> 00:20:47,000
Why does our usual breakfast
taste so good today?

363
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,367
I guess that's
what happens when

364
00:20:49,467 --> 00:20:54,133
your enemy hasn't slept
all night because of fear.

365
00:20:54,133 --> 00:20:55,167
[CHUCKLES]

366
00:20:55,167 --> 00:20:58,233
Let's see if the NCIA
will go after us now.

367
00:20:58,233 --> 00:21:00,833
I saw a lot of people die
last night.

368
00:21:00,833 --> 00:21:03,200
Even the head of the NCIA
was hit.

369
00:21:03,200 --> 00:21:06,967
They'll think twice now
before they retaliate.

370
00:21:06,967 --> 00:21:09,000
One more point for us.

371
00:21:09,033 --> 00:21:12,833
Good job, Lucas.

372
00:21:12,833 --> 00:21:15,433
But it would've been better
if Django's group had done it,

373
00:21:15,433 --> 00:21:18,000
so they wouldn't find out
we attacked.

374
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,233
But I'm sure
we've taken them down.

375
00:21:20,233 --> 00:21:22,900
And they won't be able to
get back on their feet.

376
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:24,500
Thank you, Papa.

377
00:21:24,567 --> 00:21:29,367
But you should've
killed everyone.

378
00:21:29,367 --> 00:21:33,100
Next time, leave no witnesses.

379
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:35,733
No loose ends.

380
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:39,833
Relax, Mariano.

381
00:21:39,833 --> 00:21:43,400
The NCIA is down on its knees.

382
00:21:43,433 --> 00:21:49,267
Let them hold on
to the sliver of hope

383
00:21:49,267 --> 00:21:51,933
that they can recover from this.

384
00:21:53,033 --> 00:21:57,267
By the time they make a move,
we'll be ten steps ahead.

385
00:21:57,267 --> 00:22:04,233
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

386
00:22:05,533 --> 00:22:07,767
- [PIA] Sir?
- Yeah?

387
00:22:10,267 --> 00:22:12,900
- This is for you.
- Oh...

388
00:22:12,900 --> 00:22:14,067
Thank you.

389
00:22:15,933 --> 00:22:17,400
Are you okay?

390
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:18,467
Mm-hmm.

391
00:22:19,833 --> 00:22:21,400
How are you?

392
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:23,067
I'm fine.

393
00:22:25,467 --> 00:22:28,833
Were there a lot
of casualties last night?

394
00:22:28,833 --> 00:22:32,033
Sir, don't worry about that
for now.

395
00:22:32,633 --> 00:22:34,933
[CLICKS TONGUE]
Focus on your recovery.

396
00:22:34,933 --> 00:22:36,500
Forget about the agency.

397
00:22:36,500 --> 00:22:39,100
Focus on healing.

398
00:22:39,100 --> 00:22:41,167
Even without me,

399
00:22:41,167 --> 00:22:43,967
the NCIA must continue
its operations.

400
00:22:43,967 --> 00:22:47,067
The enemy
will make another move.

401
00:22:48,467 --> 00:22:50,467
We cannot stop.

402
00:22:50,467 --> 00:22:52,467
You will continue the work.

403
00:22:52,467 --> 00:22:53,833
And most importantly,

404
00:22:54,867 --> 00:22:57,167
don't be discouraged.

405
00:22:57,167 --> 00:22:58,333
You can count on us.

406
00:22:59,433 --> 00:23:02,600
We will uncover the truth

407
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:05,467
and hold the culprit
accountable.

408
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:12,433
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

409
00:23:15,467 --> 00:23:17,000
- [LAUGHTER]
- What is he wearing?

410
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:20,267
- Nice fit, Gabo!
- Wow!

411
00:23:20,267 --> 00:23:21,467
- Gabo!
- What?

412
00:23:21,500 --> 00:23:23,067
Whose funeral are you
going to?

413
00:23:23,067 --> 00:23:24,333
[LAUGHTER]

414
00:23:24,333 --> 00:23:26,333
- Hey!
- Just kidding!

415
00:23:26,333 --> 00:23:28,033
You look great, Gabo!

416
00:23:28,033 --> 00:23:29,367
Looking sharp, man!

417
00:23:29,367 --> 00:23:31,333
That jacket really suits you.

418
00:23:31,333 --> 00:23:32,833
- You look cool.
- Of course!

419
00:23:32,833 --> 00:23:35,067
You thought I was
Keanu Reeves, didn't you?

420
00:23:35,067 --> 00:23:37,167
- [EXCLAIMS]
- I don't like it.

421
00:23:37,167 --> 00:23:38,833
I still prefer the old Gabo.

422
00:23:38,833 --> 00:23:41,233
- Tekla.
- What?

423
00:23:41,233 --> 00:23:43,667
Why'd you let him do this,
Miss Mameng?

424
00:23:43,667 --> 00:23:44,567
What do you guys think?

425
00:23:44,567 --> 00:23:46,200
- Looking good!
- Handsome!

426
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:47,533
Well, of course!

427
00:23:47,533 --> 00:23:48,633
My wife dressed me.

428
00:23:48,633 --> 00:23:51,533
- [EXCLAIMING]
- [TEKLA] No wonder.

429
00:23:51,533 --> 00:23:53,633
Why did you let her?

430
00:23:54,533 --> 00:23:56,633
- All right, boys.
- That's Tekla.

431
00:23:56,667 --> 00:23:58,367
I'll go look for a job.

432
00:23:58,367 --> 00:23:59,567
Stay here.

433
00:23:59,567 --> 00:24:01,200
Look after Gloria, all right?

434
00:24:01,200 --> 00:24:02,567
- Okay, Gabo.
- We got this.

435
00:24:02,567 --> 00:24:05,067
- Wow!
- Look at Betchay!

436
00:24:05,067 --> 00:24:06,200
- Wow!
- Whoa!

437
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:08,267
- You look great, Betchay!
- Oh, really?

438
00:24:08,267 --> 00:24:10,700
Would you look at that?!
Beautiful!

439
00:24:10,700 --> 00:24:13,167
- Oh, come on.
- Wow!

440
00:24:13,767 --> 00:24:17,400
- Wow, Betchay.
- She looks like Alicia Mayer!

441
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:19,400
- What?
- No, Tolits.

442
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:22,867
She looks more like
Ms. Alma Moreno!

443
00:24:22,867 --> 00:24:24,533
- Really?
- [BETCHAY LAUGHING]

444
00:24:24,533 --> 00:24:25,667
[MAMENG] Betchay?

445
00:24:25,667 --> 00:24:27,400
Is that you?

446
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:30,100
What happened?!

447
00:24:30,133 --> 00:24:31,767
- [SCOFFS]
- Wow, Betchay.

448
00:24:31,767 --> 00:24:33,400
You look 20 years younger.

449
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:34,733
Betchay, is that really you?

450
00:24:34,733 --> 00:24:38,700
You look like a jaundiced fish.

451
00:24:38,700 --> 00:24:41,200
- Are those scales?
- Excuse me!

452
00:24:41,200 --> 00:24:42,867
Calm down, calm down.

453
00:24:42,867 --> 00:24:46,300
This is Betchay.

454
00:24:46,300 --> 00:24:49,767
[TOLITS] Tell us, Miss Betchay.
Did you win the lottery?

455
00:24:49,767 --> 00:24:51,433
Or did you find
a foreign boyfriend?

456
00:24:51,433 --> 00:24:53,467
- [BETCHAY LAUGHING]
- Did you win at a game?

457
00:24:53,467 --> 00:24:55,733
[BETCHAY] No, I didn't.

458
00:24:55,733 --> 00:25:00,467
I had a very generous
customer last night.

459
00:25:00,467 --> 00:25:02,533
He gave me a huge tip...

460
00:25:02,567 --> 00:25:05,500
- ...for a job well done.
- Oh...

461
00:25:05,500 --> 00:25:08,933
Are you wearing real jewelry?

462
00:25:08,933 --> 00:25:10,467
Of course not! [SCOFFS]

463
00:25:10,467 --> 00:25:13,900
They only look legit
because I'm wearing them.

464
00:25:13,900 --> 00:25:15,667
[DIDAY] Is that so?

465
00:25:15,667 --> 00:25:18,467
[GASPS] Oh!

466
00:25:18,467 --> 00:25:20,300
Gabo.

467
00:25:20,300 --> 00:25:22,667
What a nice outfit!

468
00:25:22,667 --> 00:25:24,433
It put mine to shame.

469
00:25:24,433 --> 00:25:25,900
Where are you off to?

470
00:25:26,733 --> 00:25:28,200
Um...

471
00:25:28,767 --> 00:25:31,400
I'm going to look for a job.

472
00:25:31,400 --> 00:25:34,300
You told me
I should have a decent job

473
00:25:34,300 --> 00:25:36,300
once I got married.

474
00:25:36,333 --> 00:25:38,433
So I'm going to find one.

475
00:25:40,433 --> 00:25:41,833
[INHALES DEEPLY,
EXHALES SHARPLY]

476
00:25:41,833 --> 00:25:44,800
Okay, well, good luck.

477
00:25:44,800 --> 00:25:48,667
I hope you find a job,
not trouble.

478
00:25:48,667 --> 00:25:50,533
Good luck!

479
00:25:50,533 --> 00:25:52,433
[GIGGLES]

480
00:25:52,433 --> 00:25:56,600
- Looky, looky, looky, looky!
- Are those canned sardines?

481
00:25:56,667 --> 00:25:58,467
Excuse me?

482
00:25:58,467 --> 00:26:00,600
These are imported products.

483
00:26:00,667 --> 00:26:01,800
Corned beef.

484
00:26:01,800 --> 00:26:02,933
- Wow.
- Corned beef?

485
00:26:02,933 --> 00:26:04,633
- Did you hear that?
- Whoa.

486
00:26:04,633 --> 00:26:05,833
Corned beef.

487
00:26:05,833 --> 00:26:07,333
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

488
00:26:08,667 --> 00:26:11,400
Gabo, good luck
with your job hunting.

489
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:15,067
Remember, it's okay
to be nervous, but don't be.

490
00:26:15,067 --> 00:26:16,167
Huh?

491
00:26:17,133 --> 00:26:19,100
I'll get going, love.

492
00:26:19,733 --> 00:26:21,967
Auntie, Papa, I'll go ahead now.

493
00:26:21,967 --> 00:26:23,033
Gotta beat the traffic.

494
00:26:23,033 --> 00:26:24,900
- Take care, son.
- Good luck, okay?

495
00:26:24,900 --> 00:26:26,033
Bye, my love.

496
00:26:26,033 --> 00:26:27,033
Be careful.

497
00:26:27,033 --> 00:26:28,967
Wait a minute, Gabo.

498
00:26:28,967 --> 00:26:29,900
That's it?

499
00:26:29,900 --> 00:26:31,067
Why?

500
00:26:31,067 --> 00:26:33,700
Are you not going
to give her a goodbye kiss?

501
00:26:33,700 --> 00:26:35,233
- Yeah, kiss her!
- Kiss! Kiss!

502
00:26:35,233 --> 00:26:36,800
Oh, hell no!
Absolutely not!

503
00:26:36,800 --> 00:26:38,233
That's not necessary!

504
00:26:38,233 --> 00:26:40,733
- They're husband and wife!
- So, what?!

505
00:26:40,733 --> 00:26:42,633
- They have to kiss!
- No!

506
00:26:42,667 --> 00:26:43,833
Gabo is going to be late!

507
00:26:43,833 --> 00:26:45,733
Married couples kiss!

508
00:26:45,733 --> 00:26:48,100
- Kiss! Kiss!
- Come on!

509
00:26:48,100 --> 00:26:50,433
- For good luck!
- Kiss!

510
00:26:50,433 --> 00:26:52,700
Hey, stop it, guys!

511
00:26:52,700 --> 00:26:54,033
- Kiss!
- One smack!

512
00:26:54,033 --> 00:26:56,200
- One smooch!
- Come on!

513
00:26:56,200 --> 00:26:59,000
- Do it!
- I'm begging you, Gabo!

514
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:00,433
- Don't!
- [GABO] Love?

515
00:27:00,433 --> 00:27:03,267
- Please, don't!
- Let's give 'em what they want.

516
00:27:03,267 --> 00:27:06,200
They're not going to stop
teasing you if we don't.

517
00:27:06,200 --> 00:27:09,233
- You won't get anything done.
- Oh, come on!

518
00:27:09,233 --> 00:27:11,267
- They won't stop.
- [EXCLAIMS, CHEERS]

519
00:27:11,267 --> 00:27:12,933
- Come on!
- Right here.

520
00:27:12,933 --> 00:27:13,933
- Here we go.
- Kiss!

521
00:27:13,933 --> 00:27:16,333
- Just on the cheek.
- Sure.

522
00:27:16,367 --> 00:27:18,300
- Mm-hmm.
- [GUSHING]

523
00:27:18,300 --> 00:27:19,300
Right here.

524
00:27:19,300 --> 00:27:21,833
- Let's go! Kiss, kiss!
- Come on.

525
00:27:23,100 --> 00:27:24,700
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

526
00:27:24,700 --> 00:27:29,733
[CHEERING, APPLAUSE]

527
00:27:30,767 --> 00:27:31,767
You're the man, Gabo!

528
00:27:32,767 --> 00:27:36,767
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

529
00:27:36,767 --> 00:27:38,233
Bye!

530
00:27:38,233 --> 00:27:39,233
Good luck!

531
00:27:39,233 --> 00:27:46,233
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

532
00:27:56,300 --> 00:27:59,967
I've gained the collective trust
<i> of Team Alpha.</i>

533
00:27:59,967 --> 00:28:03,433
<i>I'll be able to easily
manipulate these fools.</i>

534
00:28:03,433 --> 00:28:05,467
<i> This is so stupid!</i>

535
00:28:05,467 --> 00:28:08,633
<i>What if we just burn it
so we'll be done already?</i>

536
00:28:08,633 --> 00:28:11,167
[LOUD EXPLOSION]

537
00:28:11,167 --> 00:28:13,767
<i> This is a dangerous job.</i>

538
00:28:13,767 --> 00:28:16,767
<i>Your loved ones
could get involved.</i>

539
00:28:16,767 --> 00:28:18,767
<i>I accept the mission
to become an Anino member.</i>

540
00:28:18,767 --> 00:28:20,400
<i> Someone has to take action.</i>

541
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:21,800
<i> Someone has to start.</i>

542
00:28:21,800 --> 00:28:22,733
<i> And that's me.</i>
